.TH NOTTERIZMUS 1 "2026-11-06" "notterizmus 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notterizmus \- outline editor for book chapter notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notterizmus
.RI [ FILE.notz ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notterizmus
is a GNOME outline editor for taking notes on book chapters.
Items are numbered automatically (Roman numerals such as I, I.1, I.1.a)
and joined by tree connectors; the
.B Copy for TopCoding
button copies the outline as formatted HTML that pastes cleanly into TopCoding.
.PP
Each book chapter is stored as one autosaved
.I .notz
file under
.I Notterizmus/<Book>/
in the user's Documents folder
.RB ( XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR ,
which may have a localized name).
Without a
.I FILE
argument the last opened chapter is reopened.
.PP
Press
.B F1
in the application for Getting Started, a practice chapter that shows each
control, and
.B Ctrl+?
for the list of keyboard shortcuts.
.B F9
shows or hides the chapter list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/notterizmus/rules.toml
Optional formatting rules: numbering formats, connector characters, spacing and
bullet markers.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notterizmus/state.json
Last opened chapter, spell-checking preferences and the chapter list's
visibility and width.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/notterizmus/Getting Started.notz
The Getting Started practice copy, rewritten each time it is opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/notterizmus/FEATURES.md
.SH AUTHOR
Simo Andreev <simeon.zlatanov.andreev@pm.me>
